{
  "id": "869",
  "title": "Ben’s Diary – Sad/Difficult",
  "level": "intermediate",
  "date": "2020-02-18",
  "synopsis": "Ben is musing about the expression “nán guò”.",
  "audioUrl": "https://static.duchinese.net/documents/869/39b12a9a6ebf5bbeb8759563f7002dd02b66528c.mp3?1581779801",
  "series": null,
  "fullText": {
    "simplified": "本的日记—难过\n\n    我发现“难过”这个词特别有意思，它可以是一个词，也可以是两个词。\n    如果是一个词—“难过”，那就是“不开心”的意思。比如：丽丽不喜欢我，我很难过。\n    如果是两个词—“难/过”，那就是“很难通过”的意思。比如：HSK考试很难过。\n    哈哈！HSK考试很难过，所以我很难过。",
    "traditional": "本的日記—難過\n\n    我發現“難過”這個詞特別有意思，它可以是一個詞，也可以是兩個詞。\n    如果是一個詞—“難過”，那就是“不開心”的意思。比如：麗麗不喜歡我，我很難過。\n    如果是兩個詞—“難/過”，那就是“很難通過”的意思。比如：HSK考試很難過。\n    哈哈！HSK考試很難過，所以我很難過。"
  },
  "sentences": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "simplified": "\n\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Ben’s Diary – Sad/Difficult"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "simplified": "我发现“难过”这个词特别有意思，",
      "traditional": "我發現“難過”這個詞特別有意思，",
      "pinyin": "wǒ fā xiàn nán guò zhè ge cí tè bié yǒu yì si",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "simplified": "它可以是一个词，也可以是两个词。",
      "traditional": "它可以是一個詞，也可以是兩個詞。",
      "pinyin": "tā kě yǐ shì yí ge cí yě kě yǐ shì liǎng ge cí",
      "english": "I’ve discovered that the word “nán guò” is particularly interesting."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "It can be one word, but it can also be two words."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "simplified": "如果是一个词—“难过”，那就是“不开心”的意思。",
      "traditional": "如果是一個詞—“難過”，那就是“不開心”的意思。",
      "pinyin": "rú guǒ shì yí ge cí nán guò nà jiù shì bù kāi xīn de yì si",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "simplified": "比如：丽丽不喜欢我，我很难过。",
      "traditional": "比如：麗麗不喜歡我，我很難過。",
      "pinyin": "bǐ rú lì lì bù xǐ huan wǒ wǒ hěn nán guò",
      "english": "If it’s one word - “nánguò”, then it means “unhappy”."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "For example: Lili doesn’t like me, so I feel very sad."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "simplified": "如果是两个词—“难/过”，那就是“很难通过”的意思。",
      "traditional": "如果是兩個詞—“難/過”，那就是“很難通過”的意思。",
      "pinyin": "rú guǒ shì liǎng ge cí nán guò nà jiù shì hěn nán tōng guò de yì si",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "simplified": "比如：HSK考试很难过。",
      "traditional": "比如：HSK考試很難過。",
      "pinyin": "bǐ rú 3 kǎo shì hěn nán guò",
      "english": "If it’s two words - “nán/guò”, then it means “very hard to pass”."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "For example: The HSK exam is very hard to pass."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "simplified": "哈哈！HSK考试很难过，所以我很难过。",
      "traditional": "哈哈！HSK考試很難過，所以我很難過。",
      "pinyin": "hā hā 3 kǎo shì hěn nán guò suǒ yǐ wǒ hěn nán guò",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "simplified": "",
      "traditional": "",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Haha! The HSK exam is very hard to pass, therefore I feel very sad."
    }
  ],
